{title: God Bless Our Native Land}
{artist: Siegfried August Mahlmann · tr. Charles Timothy Brooks & John Sullivan Dwight}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
[F]God bless [Gm]our [C]native land! [F]Firm [Dm]may [Gm]she [F]ever [Dm]stand [Gm]Through [F]storm [C]and
[F]night; When [Am]the wild [F]tempests rave, [C7]Ruler of wind and [C]wave,
[F]Do [Bb]Thou [Gm7]our [F]country save [Bb]By [F]Thy [C7]great [F]might.

Verse 2
[F]For her [Gm]our [C]prayer shall rise [F]To [Dm]God [Gm]a[F]bove the [Dm]skies; [Gm]On [F]Him [C]we
[F]wait; Thou [Am]who art [F]ever nigh, [C7]Guarding with watchful [C]eye,
[F]To [Bb]Thee [Gm7]a[F]loud we cry, [Bb]God [F]save [C7]the [F]state!
